<% content_for :title, "Sources — crest" %>

<section style="padding: 30px 0 0;">
  <h1 class="display" style="font-size: 44px;">Where every number comes from</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="padding-top: 12px; max-width: 660px;">
    crest holds no private data. Every match, score, venue and goal on this site is traceable
    to an open file you can download yourself.
  </p>
</section>

<section style="padding: 30px 0 0;">
  <hr class="rule">
  <div style="padding: 22px 0;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <div>
        <h2 class="serif" style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 24px; margin: 0;">Men's internationals</h2>
        <div class="num" style="font-size: 13px; padding-top: 5px;">
          <a href="https://github.com/martj42/international_results">github.com/martj42/international_results</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align: right;">
        <div class="num" style="font-size: 15px; border: 1px solid var(--navy); color: var(--navy); padding: 5px 12px; display: inline-block;">CC0-1.0</div>
        <div class="cap" style="padding-top: 6px;">Public domain</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="num" style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.9; color: var(--ink-faint); padding-top: 16px; max-width: 820px; font-weight: 400;">
      The four files ship unmodified in this repository under <code>db/source</code>, so you can check any
      figure against the original. <strong style="color: var(--ink);"><%= number_with_delimiter @matches %> matches</strong>,
      <%= @goals %> goals and <%= @players %> scorers are the United States slice.
      Strictly men's full internationals &mdash; the source excludes Olympic Games, B-teams and
      under-23 sides, so crest does too.
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="hair">

  <div id="women" class="card" style="margin: 22px 0; border-color: var(--navy);">
    <div style="padding: 24px 24px 0;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <div>
          <h2 class="serif" style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 26px; margin: 0;">Women's internationals</h2>
          <div class="num" style="font-size: 13px; padding-top: 5px;">
            <a href="https://github.com/martj42/womens-international-results">github.com/martj42/womens-international-results</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
          <div class="num" style="font-size: 15px; background: var(--oxblood); color: var(--paper); padding: 5px 12px; display: inline-block;">NO LICENSE</div>
          <div class="cap" style="padding-top: 6px; color: var(--oxblood);">Not shipped yet</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="num" style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 2; color: var(--ink-soft); padding-top: 16px; max-width: 800px; font-weight: 400;">
        We found this dataset and want to use it. It has no license file, so we cannot ship it in an
        open repository. It is also missing a lot of matches, by its own account.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--paper); border-top: 1px solid var(--navy); margin-top: 22px; padding: 20px 24px;">
      <h3 class="serif" style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; margin: 0;">Know a better source?</h3>
      <p class="cap" style="padding-top: 6px; margin: 0;">A link is enough.</p>
      <p class="num" style="font-size: 13px; padding-top: 12px; margin: 0;">
        <a href="mailto:hi@crest.soccer?subject=A%20source%20for%20the%20women%27s%20record">hi@crest.soccer</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="rule">
</section>

<section class="split" style="gap: 0; padding: 26px 0 0;">
  <div class="divider" style="padding-right: 34px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);">
    <div class="cap" style="color: var(--navy); padding-bottom: 12px;">What crest computes</div>
    <div class="num" style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 2.1; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 400;">
      World Cup cycles &mdash; <%= ::Cycle.count %> of them<br>
      Records: won, drawn, lost, goals for and against<br>
      Scorer rankings and goals per cycle<br>
      Venue counts by city and country
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="divided" style="padding-left: 34px;">
    <div class="cap" style="color: var(--oxblood); padding-bottom: 12px;">What no source gives us</div>
    <div class="num" style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 2.1; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 400;">
      Appearances &mdash; so caps start at zero and grow<br>
      Positions, clubs, minutes played<br>
      Line-ups and substitutions<br>
      Attendance, referees, stadium names<br>
      Venue coordinates &mdash; no map without another source
    </div>
    <div class="cap" style="padding-top: 12px;">Shown as a dash, never as a zero.</div>
  </div>
</section>
